# pi coding agent: zero built-in permission system, governed anyway — the
# extension IS the whole coverage story (pi has no MCP layer, no confirm
# gate of its own). Setup tour → destructive "sanctioned" step denied at
# the hardline floor (no confirm dialog to click through, unlike claude/
# codex) → normal work still allowed → session receipt.
#
# NOT YET RECORDED. demo/episodes/pi.sh documents a real rig gap: pi's ACP
# integration is cloud-only (no local/no-signup mode), and record.sh's
# shared plumbing (Beat 1, prep(), login flow) assumes local mode
# throughout. A one-time manual credential step is required before any
# take — see the RIG GAP block at the top of demo/episodes/pi.sh. Until
# that's done, only `demo/record.sh manual pi` is viable (a human narrates
# past record.sh's irrelevant-for-pi Beat 1); `record.sh record pi`
# (unattended) is not yet trustworthy.
CAST=pi.cast

# ── everything below this line is footage-timing and can only be set from
# a real take's paced cast (youtube/README.md: "PACE windows in the .env
# are on the idle-capped, speed-1 clock" — run `build.sh beats pi` after
# `demo/record.sh manual pi` produces demo/pi.cast, then fill these in) ──
IDLE_CAP=
PACE=
TAIL_HOLD=

# Content fields — these don't depend on footage, safe to fill ahead of a
# take. Kept close to the shape of claude-install-yt/amazonq-yt so the
# pipeline scripts don't need special-casing.
TITLE1='pi ships zero permission system'
TITLE2='governed at every tool call anyway'
HOOK='no confirm dialog to click through — nothing else would have stopped this'
OUTRO2='one extension covers every tool call — pi has no MCP layer to supplement'
OUTRO_URL='agenticcontrolplane.com/controls/pi'
THUMB_TITLE='No permission system, built in — governed anyway'
THUMB_TAG='DENIED'

# ── timing windows: TBD from beats.mjs after a real take ──
COLDOPEN_START=
COLDOPEN_END=
CALLOUT_1=
CALLOUT_2=
CALLOUT_3=
CALLOUT_4=
CALLOUT_5=
SHORT_START=
SHORT_END=
THUMB_T=
